		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=42539#p42539"><![CDATA[
Yes, by default we use convex hulls. Best to create a convex decomposition for moving objects (using VHACD, there are utils from obj -&gt; vhacd).<br>See this example:<br><a href="https://github.com/bulletphysics/bullet3/blob/master/data/teddy_vhacd.urdf" class="postlink">https://github.com/bulletphysics/bullet ... vhacd.urdf</a><br><br><br>For concave static trangle meshes, you can mark them as 'concave'.<br>See samurai.urdf for an example <a href="https://github.com/bulletphysics/bullet3/blob/master/data/samurai.urdf#L3" class="postlink">https://github.com/bulletphysics/bullet ... ai.urdf#L3</a><p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=2">Erwin Coumans</a> — Fri Dec 20, 2019 12:08 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
